# How to build Sphinx documentation

Build docs from the repository root:

```bash
python3 -m venv build/
source build/bin/activate
pip install sphinx myst-parser
```

Build gem5 and move to `docs/`:

```bash
scons build/ALL/gem5.opt
cd docs
```

Generate Python API `.rst` files:

```bash
../build/ALL/gem5.opt gem5-sphinx-apidoc -o . ../src/python/gem5 -e
```

Do not pass `-F`. This repository keeps `docs/index.rst`, `docs/conf.py`,
and `docs/Makefile` under version control, and `-F` would overwrite them.

Build HTML docs:

```bash
SPHINXBUILD="../build/ALL/gem5.opt gem5-sphinx" make html
```

View locally:

```bash
cd _build/html
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

Tutorial lesson READMEs are source-adjacent in `src/tutorial/`, with the
top-level course page at `src/tutorial/README.md`.
Sphinx wrapper pages for rendering are in `docs/tutorial/`, with
`docs/tutorial/index.md` as the docs entry page.
